WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.662
Look, I think the system

2
00:00:03.653 --> 00:00:09.750
is a combination of action
and inaction by the world's governments.

3
00:00:11.498 --> 00:00:16.077
They usually say it's to help humanity,
society, the individual.

4
00:00:16.161 --> 00:00:17.858
But the way things are going,

5
00:00:17.942 --> 00:00:21.681
you can see that everything
the system does is against people,

6
00:00:21.765 --> 00:00:23.976
especially against the poor.

7
00:00:24.127 --> 00:00:28.679
Because they kind of push us
into being poor, on purpose.

8
00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:34.808
Because what is a poor person?

9
00:00:34.892 --> 00:00:39.970
A poor person is someone who doesn't
reach a certain means, a certain level.

10
00:00:40.914 --> 00:00:44.145
But it's the system
that decides who gets there.

11
00:00:44.315 --> 00:00:46.265
Because if it's about work,

12
00:00:46.349 --> 00:00:50.233
there's no people that works harder
than African people. There isn't.

13
00:00:50.317 --> 00:00:57.269
We work so much, so much, so much, only to
end up in a shack, in a self-built house.

14
00:00:57.679 --> 00:00:59.530
Mind you, our house is good.

15
00:00:59.614 --> 00:01:02.506
It's good because we
built Portugal's buildings:

16
00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:04.507
the men from here build them.

17
00:01:04.591 --> 00:01:07.175
Of course, for ourselves,
we build a good house.

18
00:01:07.259 --> 00:01:10.070
But we work so much.

19
00:01:10.154 --> 00:01:14.801
Human beings work so hard, they give
their blood to get the bare minimum.

20
00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.394
People, this is inhumane.

21
00:01:16.502 --> 00:01:20.090
What the system is doing
to people is inhumane.

22
00:01:21.006 --> 00:01:25.144
And all they put in our heads is:
"Have hope for the future."

23
00:01:25.228 --> 00:01:26.919
That future that never comes.

24
00:01:27.209 --> 00:01:29.040
That better future never comes.

25
00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:34.862
But it's the church, it's politics,
always: "Work, and God will provide.

26
00:01:34.946 --> 00:01:36.429
Work, tomorrow will be better."

27
00:01:36.513 --> 00:01:41.324
You work like a slave, and you never,
never have anything, nothing better.

28
00:01:41.915 --> 00:01:45.086
And the most incredible thing
is that people think this is normal.

29
00:01:45.356 --> 00:01:49.276
Human beings think life
is about work, work, work.

30
00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:55.496
As a child, you don't have a childhood,
you don't do anything you like as a child.

31
00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:57.110
You only do what you must.

32
00:01:57.445 --> 00:02:01.156
When you're young,
you're already pushed into work.

33
00:02:01.366 --> 00:02:06.520
As an adult, you have lots of things
to do, lots of responsibility.

34
00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:11.618
They promise you'll live
comfortably when you're old.

35
00:02:12.288 --> 00:02:14.125
With a pension that, in the end,

36
00:02:14.209 --> 00:02:19.520
isn't even enough to pay
for the costs of old age.

37
00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:23.862
Because we see it here in Portugal,
in Portugal, around the world:

38
00:02:24.274 --> 00:02:27.803
old people are suffering,
because they worked their whole lives,

39
00:02:27.887 --> 00:02:31.210
they reach old age
and the pension isn't enough for anything.

40
00:02:31.294 --> 00:02:35.546
And if human beings don't
rise up against this system,

41
00:02:36.296 --> 00:02:40.807
we'll go back to slavery again,
but a prettied-up slavery.

42
00:02:41.158 --> 00:02:46.009
A beautiful slavery, like, because
when it's the government doing the shit,

43
00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:48.270
it's all beautiful.

44
00:02:48.475 --> 00:02:52.387
The name for slavery is democracy.

45
00:02:52.569 --> 00:02:55.235
Like, they give something
horrible a beautiful name,

46
00:02:55.319 --> 00:02:59.777
and we accept it as beautiful. But what's
happening in the world is inhumane.

47
00:02:59.861 --> 00:03:02.819
What the system is doing
to people is inhumane,

48
00:03:02.903 --> 00:03:07.976
because they push people into poverty.
From childhood, they put it in our heads.

49
00:03:08.266 --> 00:03:12.538
And when we stand up
to rebel against poverty,

50
00:03:12.768 --> 00:03:14.919
you see there's no way out.

51
00:03:15.949 --> 00:03:18.888
Or, if there is a way out,
you need a lot of emotional support,

52
00:03:18.972 --> 00:03:22.885
you have to be really well
prepared to get out of poverty.

53
00:03:23.535 --> 00:03:26.453
Because it's programmed,
it's from childhood.

54
00:03:26.537 --> 00:03:31.491
They make us poor and then they blame us.

55
00:03:31.848 --> 00:03:36.554
They give us this feeling of guilt,
that we're the ones not doing anything,

56
00:03:36.638 --> 00:03:39.052
but we're doing everything,
because we work.
